WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:01.480
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
What's up, everyone?

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:03.980
Thanks for checking out "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.940
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.039
Many teams are looking
at Kubernetes and Istio

00:00:08.039 --> 00:00:09.965
to help manage their
complex applications.

00:00:09.965 --> 00:00:11.340
But they still
come up short when

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.490
they're trying to implement and
host the actual infrastructure.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.710
At Google Cloud
Next 2018, we first

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.510
introduced the simple
but radical idea

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.760
of a less disruptive
and more compliant

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.288
Services Platform built
entirely on open APIs.

00:00:24.288 --> 00:00:25.830
We couldn't be more
proud to announce

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.080
that Google Cloud
Services Platform is

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.760
open to everyone in beta.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.280
If you're currently using
Kubernetes or running a hybrid

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.170
of on-prem and in
the cloud, you now

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.760
have a powerful
tool to modernize

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.100
existing apps at your own pace.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.740
Google Kubernetes Engine is
the industry-leading managed

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.170
Kubernetes service, letting
you focus on your application

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.730
and configuration
without worrying

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.520
about the operational
security or infrastructure.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.700
GKE On-Prem brings that same
managed Kubernetes experience

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.410
to your on-prem clusters.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.850
With Cloud Services
Platform, you

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.310
can write once and have
consistent environments,

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:59.760
plus a single source of truth
for configuration management.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.630
There is a lot to take
of advantage here.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.540
So check out the
beta and see how

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.519
CSP can help your architecture.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:07.380
Speaking of modernizing
your applications,

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.840
if you've got some Java
applications lying around,

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.670
and you want to look
at containerization,

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.320
you'll really like
the cut of our Jib.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.180
That is, Google's
open source Jib

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.597
project that helps build Java
applications into containers.

00:01:18.597 --> 00:01:20.430
You can easily integrate
with Maven, Gradle,

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.710
or by using the
library directly.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.393
Jib was just pushed
to version 1.0

00:01:24.393 --> 00:01:25.560
and is now production ready.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.270
So get building.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.160
Even still, migrating
applications

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.598
can be a ton of work.

00:01:30.598 --> 00:01:32.640
Last year, Google announced
that we're teaming up

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.800
with Velostrata to help
people make that migration

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.190
process a lot easier.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:39.030
And now we're looking to team
up with illuma, experts in data

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.960
migration and integration.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:43.530
So if you need some support
in migrating to the cloud,

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.300
or just want to build
a data pipeline,

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.740
Google and illuma
have your back.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.310
So we've been talking a lot
about Google Cloud Next and all

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.050
the cool things that are
going to be shown off there.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.430
But here's one more cool thing.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.680
You can get a free
ticket to Next.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.500
Google has released some new
certifications and Qwiklabs

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.120
content to go along with those.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.370
Not only can you get one
month free of Qwiklabs

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.680
and get your hands-on
training, but you'll then

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.080
receive a discount for
the certification exam.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.240
Then if you get
certified by March 31,

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.025
you'll get a free pass to Next.

00:02:11.025 --> 00:02:12.150
There's no reason to delay.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.597
So get started now and
unlock your cloud potential.

00:02:14.597 --> 00:02:16.680
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.960
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.160
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.910
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.320
We'll see you in the cloud.

